---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
import Skull from '../components/Skull.astro';
---
<Base title="Bare Bones SEO Controls for AI-Built Websites" description="Bare Bones SEO opens the black box of AI-built websites, giving you visibility, consistency, and control over technical SEO settings—not optimization advice.">
  <section class="product-hero wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Bare Bones SEO</a>
    <h1><span class="heading-mark"><Skull size={48} /></span>Bare Bones SEO for AI-built websites</h1>
    <p class="lede">Open the black box. Put the SEO practitioner in the driver’s seat.</p>
    <p class="intro">See the SEO settings your AI built, control them directly, and keep them consistent through future changes. Bare Bones SEO provides open-source standards your agent implements using your site’s existing framework and host.</p>
    <div class="product-actions">
      <a class="product-button" href={site.staticGithub}>Get the standards on GitHub ↗</a>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Free and open source. Not a plugin or a one-click installer.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section install-section" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="install-title">Copy this into your AI website builder</h2>
      <p class="install-intro">Use this when building a new static website or adding Bare Bones to an existing one. Your AI agent needs access to the public GitHub repository.</p>
      <div class="prompt-box">
        <div class="prompt-toolbar">
          <span>Installation instructions</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-prompt" data-copy-prompt aria-label="Copy Bare Bones SEO installation instructions">Copy prompt</button>
        </div>
        <textarea id="install-prompt" readonly rows="9" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Bare Bones SEO installation prompt">Follow the Bare Bones SEO for Static Sites standards:
https://github.com/charltondigital/bare-bones-seo-static-sites

Read the README and all applicable standards before building or changing this website. Use the existing framework, host, and build tools. Consult the relevant platform playbooks for guidance, but do not install GitHub Actions, Cloudflare, Node.js, or any other tool merely to comply.

Implement the required SEO controls for metadata, indexation, sitemaps, canonical URLs, redirects, and advisory checks. Preserve existing URLs and intentional SEO settings. Verify the actual generated HTML, sitemap, and redirect behavior—not just configuration files.

Create or update AGENTS.md so future AI coding agents know to follow these standards. Be my conversational SEO dashboard: tell me what settings and reports you can show, and offer relevant views during SEO work. Leave optimization strategy and content decisions to me unless I ask for help.</textarea>
        <p class="copy-feedback" data-copy-feedback role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section comparison-section" aria-labelledby="comparison-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="comparison-heading">
        <h2 id="comparison-title">Your AI can build a website. But who’s watching the SEO?</h2>
        <p>AI coding agents aren't necessarily looking out for technical SEO. They may overlook it, scatter settings across files, or unintentionally undo decisions during later edits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="risk-benefit">
        <div class="risk-col">
          <h3>Without clear SEO standards</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>SEO may be overlooked.</strong> An AI agent focused on design or functionality may never check the indexation, metadata, or sitemap.</li>
            <li><strong>Settings can be hard to find.</strong> Titles, canonicals, and indexing rules may be scattered or duplicated.</li>
            <li><strong>Future edits can break things.</strong> A redesign or refactor may change URLs, overwrite settings, or drop redirects without warning.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="benefit-col">
          <h3>With Bare Bones SEO</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Transparency.</strong> Ask your agent to show what your site actually outputs, including titles, canonicals, indexation, and sitemaps.</li>
            <li><strong>Control.</strong> Keep technical SEO decisions in authoritative settings that you can inspect and change through conversation.</li>
            <li><strong>Consistency.</strong> Persistent instructions and advisory checks help preserve decisions and flag unexpected changes.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="comparison-note">Bare Bones doesn't make SEO decisions for you or guarantee that AI never makes mistakes. It gives your AI agent a shared specification to follow and checks to help you spot problems.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap ending">
      <h2>Not an SEO optimization tool.</h2>
      <p>You, your AI agent, or other SEO tools handle optimization—choosing keywords, improving content, and deciding what should rank. Bare Bones handles the transparency and control: showing what your site actually outputs, making technical settings manageable, and keeping those decisions consistent. No keyword scores, prescribed optimizations, extra dashboard, or required hosting migration.</p>
      <a href={site.staticGithub}>Read Bare Bones SEO for Static Sites ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<script>
  const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-prompt]');
  const prompt = document.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>('#install-prompt');
  const feedback = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-copy-feedback]');
  button?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    if (!prompt) return;
    try {
      if (navigator.clipboard?.writeText) {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(prompt.value);
      } else {
        prompt.focus();
        prompt.select();
        if (!document.execCommand('copy')) throw new Error('Copy not supported');
      }
      if (feedback) feedback.textContent = 'Copied. Paste this into your AI coding agent.';
    } catch {
      prompt.focus();
      prompt.select();
      if (feedback) feedback.textContent = 'Select and copy the highlighted instructions.';
    }
  });
</script>
<style>
  .heading-mark{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-.035em;margin-right:.2em;line-height:1}
  .heading-mark :global(svg){display:block;width:.82em;height:.82em}

  .product-hero{padding-block:var(--space-5) var(--space-6)}
  .back-link{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:var(--space-3);font-size:.92rem;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  h1{font-size:clamp(2.8rem,7vw,5rem);max-width:16ch}
  .lede{margin-top:var(--space-3);font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:600}
  .intro{margin-top:var(--space-2);max-width:38rem;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .product-actions{margin-top:var(--space-4)}
  .product-button{display:inline-block;padding:.8rem 1.15rem;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);text-decoration:none;border-radius:3px;font-weight:600}
  .note{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:var(--space-2)}
  .install-intro{color:var(--ink-soft);max-width:42rem;margin-top:var(--space-2);margin-bottom:var(--space-3)}
  .prompt-box{border:1px solid var(--line);max-width:52rem}
  .prompt-toolbar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:.75rem 1rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.9rem;font-weight:600}
  .copy-prompt{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);border:0;border-radius:3px;padding:.65rem 1rem;font:inherit;cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap}
  .copy-prompt:hover{background:var(--plate)}
  .copy-prompt:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--plate);outline-offset:3px}
  #install-prompt{display:block;width:100%;min-height:19rem;padding:1rem;background:transparent;color:var(--ink);border:0;resize:vertical;font: .91rem/1.55 var(--sans)}
  .copy-feedback{min-height:1.6rem;padding:.2rem 1rem .5rem;font-size:.86rem;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3.5vw,2.5rem)}
  .comparison-heading{max-width:47rem;margin-bottom:var(--space-3)}
  .comparison-heading p{margin-top:var(--space-2);color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .risk-benefit{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}
  .risk-col,.benefit-col{padding:clamp(1.25rem,3vw,2rem);border:1px solid var(--line)}
  .risk-col{background:var(--paper)}
  .benefit-col{background:rgba(80,117,153,.095);border-color:rgba(80,117,153,.25)}
  .risk-benefit h3{font-size:1.35rem;margin-bottom:1.25rem}
  .risk-benefit ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:1.3rem}
  .risk-benefit li{line-height:1.55;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .risk-benefit strong{display:block;color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:.25rem}
  .comparison-note{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:var(--space-3);max-width:49rem}
  .ending{display:grid;gap:1rem}
  .ending p{max-width:39rem;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .ending a{font-weight:600}
  @media(max-width:44rem){.risk-benefit{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
